===New Zealand Labour Party (32)===
The [[New Zealand Labour Party|Labour Party]] won 25.13% of the vote, entitling it to 32 seats. As it won 27 electorates, an additional 5 members were taken from the party list. After the resignation of [[David Shearer]] in [[2017 Mount Albert by-election|December 2016]], the party's share of seats was reduced to 31 until [[Raymond Huo]] was sworn in<!--not a mistake--> in March 2017.

Three new Labour Party members were elected from the list. 29 members from the 50th Parliament were returned.
